## ETHICS ADDENDUM — Defensive Use Only

This software is released under the MIT License above, **subject to the following ethical addendum** which forms an inseparable part of the license grant:

### 1. Defensive Purpose Only
The Software is designed, implemented, and licensed exclusively for **civil-defense, shelter-guidance, and situational-awareness** purposes. It fuses open, receive-only sensor data to produce a defensive operating picture. It **cannot** and **must not** be used, modified, or extended to:

- Compute aimpoints, fire-control solutions, or intercept trajectories
- Control, cue, or launch any weapon, interceptor, effector, or kinetic/non-kinetic effector
- Perform electronic attack, jamming, spoofing, or any RF emission
- Conduct targeting, battle-damage assessment, or kill-chain functions
- Enable any offensive military or coercive capability

### 2. Technical Enforcement
The Software contains programmatic safeguards (type-system constraints, test suite, runtime assertions) that **fail the build** if fire-control types, weapons buses, aimpoint geometry, intercept modules, or transmitter classes are introduced. These safeguards are integral to the Software and must not be removed, disabled, or circumvented.

### 3. No Transmitter / Emitter Designs
The Software includes no transmitter schematics, exciter designs, RF power-amplifier layouts, or emission-control logic. The CAD model (`cad/palladium-null-array.cad.json`) explicitly declares `interfaces.weapons === null` and `compliance.transmitter === "none"`.

### 4. Open Data Only
The Software processes only publicly available, open-source data streams (ADS-B, AIS, METAR, USGS, GNSS integrity, FIRMS-class IR, TLEs). It does not ingest classified, restricted, or proprietary sensor feeds.

### 5. Dual-Use Acknowledgement
The physics implemented herein (Doppler, TDOA, radio horizon, SNR, orbital mechanics) is dual-use by nature. The authors acknowledge this danger and have deliberately architected the Software to **only** traverse the defensive path. Users bear responsibility for ensuring their deployments remain within the defensive envelope.

### 6. License Termination
Any use, modification, or distribution of the Software that violates this Addendum automatically terminates the license grant. The Software reverts to “All Rights Reserved” for the violating party.

### 7. No Warranty of Safety
The Software is provided “AS IS” without warranty of any kind. The defensive architecture does not guarantee safety in operational environments. Operators must validate all outputs against independent sources before acting on shelter directives.

### 8. Attribution
Derivative works must retain this Ethics Addendum verbatim in their LICENSE file and in any distributed binary or container image.

